# Secrets

- Never commit real Wi-Fi SSIDs/passwords, MQTT usernames/passwords, `.env`, `.env.*` (except `.env.example`), `credentials.json`, private keys, or auth tokens.
- Keep placeholders in `config.gleam` (or similar) in git — e.g. `YOUR_WIFI` / `YOUR_PASSWORD`. Edit locally for flash; do not commit real values.
- Never log credentials, PSKs, or tokens. Redact if a dump would include them.
- Don't hardcode secrets in source, tests, or chat replies.
- Don't paste production dumps, live tokens, or private keys into the conversation.
